Sam: Not really. I have a big maths test tomorrow and I can''t stop worrying.
Mia: I know that feeling. My hands always go cold and sweaty before a test.
Sam: Mine too. Last night I couldn''t sleep at all.
Mia: Have you tried taking a few short breaks while you study?
Sam: No. I just study for hours until my head aches.
Mia: That makes it worse. Try a ten-minute break every hour and breathe slowly.
Sam: That sounds simple. I''ll give it a try tonight.
Mia: And remember, a little stress is normal. It can even help you focus.', 'Mia 发现 Sam 很累;Sam 明天有数学大考,担心得睡不着;Mia 也会考前手脚冰冷出汗;Mia 建议学习时每小时休息十分钟并慢慢呼吸;Sam 决定试试;Mia 提醒一点压力是正常的,还能帮助集中注意力。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why is Sam worried?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He has a big maths test tomorrow.","He has lost his homework.","He had an argument with Mia.","He is moving to a new school."]},{"q":"What happens to Mia before a test?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She feels very hungry.","Her hands go cold and sweaty.","She falls asleep at once.","She forgets her name."]},{"q":"What does Mia suggest Sam do while studying?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Take short breaks and breathe slowly.","Study all night without stopping.","Skip the test completely.","Drink lots of coffee."]},{"q":"How does Sam react to Mia''s advice?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He laughs at it.","He decides to try it that night.","He refuses to listen.","He gets angry with her."]},{"q":"What does Mia say about a little stress?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It always makes you ill.","It should be ignored completely.","It is normal and can help you focus.","It never affects students."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U1', 'sufe');
Good stress shows up when you are called on in class or give a report.
A small amount of it can even help you prepare well.
Bad stress happens when worried feelings last for a long time.
That kind of stress can make you sick if you do not deal with it.', '并非所有压力都是坏的;被点名回答或做报告时出现的是好压力;少量好压力甚至能帮你做好准备;当担忧持续很久时就成了坏压力;如果不加处理,坏压力会让你生病。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the passage mainly about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["How to pass a maths test.","Why students like homework.","The best food for breakfast.","The difference between good and bad stress."]},{"q":"When might good stress show up?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["When you are called on or give a report.","When you are sleeping.","When you are on holiday.","When you are eating lunch."]},{"q":"What can a small amount of good stress do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Make you fall asleep.","Help you prepare well.","Make you forget everything.","Make you feel ill at once."]},{"q":"When does stress become bad?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["When it lasts only one minute.","When it happens before a party.","When the worried feelings last a long time.","When it makes you happy."]},{"q":"What can bad stress do if you ignore it?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It can make you taller.","It can give you more friends.","It can improve your marks.","It can make you sick."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U1', 'sufe');
Leo: Yes. Lately I feel anxious all the time, even when nothing is wrong.
Counsellor: I see. Do you have trouble sleeping or paying attention?
Leo: Both. I keep checking my homework again and again.
Counsellor: Thank you for being honest. Admitting it is already a brave first step.
Leo: So what can I do?
Counsellor: Let''s start with a balanced plan: enough sleep, some exercise, and time to relax.
Leo: That sounds manageable.
Counsellor: And if the worry stays too strong, we can talk again or see a doctor.', '心理老师请 Leo 进来谈话;Leo 说最近总是焦虑,哪怕没出事;他睡不好、注意力差,还反复检查作业;老师肯定他的坦诚,说承认问题已是勇敢的第一步;建议从平衡作息开始:充足睡眠、适当运动、留出放松时间;若担忧仍太强,可再谈或看医生。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Leo visit the counsellor?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He feels anxious even when nothing is wrong.","He wants to change his timetable.","He lost his school bag.","He needs help with sports."]},{"q":"What is one sign Leo mentions?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He sleeps too deeply.","He keeps checking his homework again and again.","He eats too quickly.","He never feels tired."]},{"q":"What does the counsellor say about admitting the problem?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is a waste of time.","It is something to be ashamed of.","It is already a brave first step.","It will make things worse."]},{"q":"What does the counsellor suggest starting with?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Giving up all homework.","Studying through the night.","Avoiding all his friends.","A balanced plan of sleep, exercise and rest."]},{"q":"What will they do if the worry stays too strong?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Talk again or see a doctor.","Forget about it completely.","Stop coming to school.","Tell no one at all."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U1', 'sufe');
Breathe in slowly through your nose and then breathe out through your mouth.
You can do this anywhere, and no one will even notice.
Listening to gentle music or doing some yoga also helps.
Choose the one that works for you and practise it often.', '给你一个惊慌时快速平静下来的方法:用鼻子慢慢吸气,再用嘴呼气;这随时随地都能做,没人会察觉;听轻柔的音乐或做点瑜伽也有帮助;选一个适合自己的方法并经常练习。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When is this quick way useful?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["When you are very hungry.","When you feel panicky.","When you want to run fast.","When you are sound asleep."]},{"q":"How should you breathe in?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Quickly through your mouth.","Not at all.","Slowly through your nose.","Only after eating."]},{"q":"What is special about this method?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It costs a lot of money.","It needs special tools.","It only works at night.","You can do it anywhere without being noticed."]},{"q":"What else does the speaker say can help?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Gentle music or some yoga.","Shouting loudly.","Skipping meals.","Staying up late."]},{"q":"What advice does the speaker give at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Try nothing at all.","Choose one method and practise it often.","Use every method at once.","Wait until you are ill."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U1', 'sufe');
Jack: More study, I suppose. I have so much to finish.
Emma: That sounds stressful. You really need a balanced weekend.
Jack: What do you mean by balanced?
Emma: Keep your SELF in mind: Sleep, Exercise, Leisure and Food.
Jack: So I shouldn''t just sit at my desk the whole time?
Emma: Exactly. Sleep well, go for a run, see your friends, and eat properly.
Jack: When you put it like that, it makes sense.
Emma: A rested mind works far better than a tired one anyway.', 'Emma 问 Jack 周末计划;Jack 说还想继续学习;Emma 说那太累了,他需要平衡的周末;她解释 SELF:睡眠、运动、休闲、饮食;建议别整天坐书桌前,要好好睡、去跑步、见朋友、好好吃饭;Jack 觉得有道理;Emma 说休息好的大脑比疲惫的大脑高效得多。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was Jack planning to do all weekend?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Travel to another city.","Sleep for two days.","Study the whole time.","Play games all day."]},{"q":"What does Emma say Jack needs?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["More tests.","A new desk.","Less sleep.","A balanced weekend."]},{"q":"What do the letters SELF stand for?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Sleep, Exercise, Leisure and Food.","Study, Energy, Luck and Faith.","Speed, Effort, Love and Fun.","School, Email, Lunch and Friends."]},{"q":"What does Emma suggest Jack do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Sit at his desk all day.","Sleep well, run, see friends and eat properly.","Skip every meal.","Stay awake all night."]},{"q":"What does Emma say about a rested mind?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is worse than a tired one.","It cannot study at all.","It works far better than a tired one.","It needs no food."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U1', 'sufe');
Talking to a parent or teacher you trust can really help.
Saying your worries out loud often makes them feel lighter.
A trusted adult may even have ideas you had not thought of.
Remember, asking for help is a sign of strength, not weakness.', '当有事让你担忧时,别全憋在心里;向你信任的父母或老师倾诉真的有用;把担忧说出来常会让它变轻;信任的大人甚至会给出你没想到的办法;记住,求助是力量的表现,不是软弱。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the speaker tell you not to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Talk to your friends.","Go to sleep early.","Eat healthy food.","Keep your worries all inside."]},{"q":"Who does the speaker suggest talking to?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A parent or teacher you trust.","A complete stranger.","Nobody at all.","Only your pet."]},{"q":"What happens when you say your worries out loud?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They grow much bigger.","They often feel lighter.","They disappear forever at once.","They turn into anger."]},{"q":"What might a trusted adult give you?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["More homework.","A reason to worry.","Ideas you had not thought of.","A long lecture."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about asking for help?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It is something to be ashamed of.","It never works.","It is only for adults.","It is a sign of strength, not weakness."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U1', 'sufe');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='sufe' AND volume='elective3' AND unit='U1';

I''m sorry to hear that you have been feeling so stressed about your studies lately. I know how hard it can be when you cannot sleep or focus, so I''d like to share a few tips that might help.

To have a balanced life is the best way to fight stress. The first thing you could try is to keep a regular routine, with enough sleep and some exercise every day. Going for a short run really clears the mind. My favourite tip is to breathe slowly and deeply whenever you feel panicky. It is also important to talk about your worries with someone you trust, like a parent or a teacher.

Don''t worry — things will get better. You are stronger than you think!

Yours,
Li Hua', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["To have a balanced life is the best way to fight stress.","The first thing you could try is to keep a regular routine.","My favourite tip is to breathe slowly and deeply whenever you feel panicky.","It is also important to talk about your worries with someone you trust."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"To having a balanced life is important.","correct":"To have a balanced life is important.","note":"不定式作主语用 to do(动词原形),不能写 to having。"},{"wrong":"It is important talk to a friend.","correct":"It is important to talk to a friend.","note":"形式主语 it 后,真正主语用不定式 to talk。"},{"wrong":"My advice is breathe slowly.","correct":"My advice is to breathe slowly.","note":"be 后作表语用不定式 to breathe。"}]'::jsonb, '【应对压力建议信结构】
称呼:Dear Alan,
第1段 关心:I''m sorry to hear that … I know how hard it can be …
第2段 建议:To have a balanced life is … The first thing you could try is to … It is important to …
第3段 鼓励:Don''t worry — things will get better!
落款:Yours, Li Hua', 2, 'elective3', 'U1', 'sufe');

